# Memcheck suppressions for scripts/valgrind-sweep.sh — the release's valgrind gate.
#
# One entry, and it names a DELIBERATE allocation: a declared text field default is interned
# for the life of the process by an intentional, bounded `Box::leak` in
# `typedef::fold_declared_default` — one allocation per field that declares a text default,
# never one per read — because `Content::Str` is a raw `{ptr, len}` with no owning variant.
# The function carries `#[inline(never)]` so this frame keeps its name; the ASan leak gate
# names the same frame in .github/lsan_suppressions.txt for the same reason.
#
# Nothing else is suppressed here on purpose.  The LSan file also suppresses the four text
# construction entry points (`append_text`, `format_text`, `format_long`, `text_tl_fmt`) on
# the premise that they leak only on a FAULT path; measured 2026-09-04 under this sweep, 14
# of the 22 scripts losing an `append_text` block carry no fault at all, so that premise does
# not hold and the class stays visible here until it is understood.
{
   declared-text-default-is-interned-for-the-process
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   ...
   fun:*fold_declared_default*
}
